                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is the type of game where you find a fascinating object on your radar screen and then you sneeze and realize the \"fascinating object\" was a cookie crumb on the screen.\n\nIt's also the type of game where the first \"real\" quest you get can be repeated endlessly to get endless credits.  And maybe I'm dumb but the description of the situation in the quest made no sense to me.  I think that if they had presented it visually it would have much more sense, but since everything in this game is shoved into the forced \"text only with choose-your-own-adventure choices\" I guess it wasn't technically possible.\n\nIt's also the type of game where fuel is really important but if you run out of fuel you can always fly to the nearest system because \"modern space drives don't need much fuel\".\n\nI can't recommend this game to anyone except people who don't mind reading lots of words that are sometimes confusing and that have many unfunny \"jokes\" throughout.",
